# Issue: the BSV parser's imperative desugaring listed a block's updated
# variables in Ord Id order, i.e. string-intern order, so the tuple that
# threads them through the desugared code, and the .bo, depended on what
# the process had compiled before.
# Fix: the variables are listed by each name's first sighting in the file.
# Probe: reuse the existing ImperativeFunctionFor.bsv syntax test (whose loop
# updates y and x) behind a Classic scrambler that interns x before y, and
# under -trace-intern-reverse; the .bo dumps must match.

copy ../../bsc.syntax/bsv05/ImperativeFunctionFor.bsv ImperativeFunctionFor.bsv
batching_bo_pair ImperativeFunctionFor.bsv LoopOrderRoot.bs LoopOrderScramble.bs
reverse_intern_same_bo ImperativeFunctionFor.bsv
erase ImperativeFunctionFor.bsv
